            "type": "text",
            "text": "Here's a slider you can drag: change the flash rate, and the count for a 12-second stretch updates immediately.\n\n```openui lifecycle=resumable id=stage-light-flash-rate\n\nroot = LearningSurface([sim], \"Stage light flash rate\", \"Drag the rate to change how many flashes occur in 12 seconds.\", \"resumable\")\nsim = Simulation(\"flash-sim\", \"Flashes in 12 seconds\", [\n  { id: \"rate\", label: \"Flash rate\", unit: \"flashes/second\", min: 1, max: 20, step: 1, value: 6 }\n], [\n  { id: \"total\", label: \"Flashes in 12 seconds\", unit: \"flashes\", expr: \"rate * 12\", precision: 0, emphasis: true },\n  { id: \"gap\", label: \"Time between flashes\", unit: \"seconds\", expr: \"1 / rate\", precision: 3 }\n], \"resumable\", \"Start by predicting how many flashes you would get at 10 flashes per second, then move the slider and check.\")\n```\n\nTry 10 flashes per second first and see whether the count matches your expectation."
          }
